WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Claude solved a nine-loop scattering amplitude problem in particle physics that stood as the prior record at eight loops. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 185, and Thropic placed a single prompt describing the nine-loop problem into its Claude science environment. The model ran largely unsupervised for days and returned a verified result. SLAC physicist Lance Dixon confirmed the output matched the expected calculation. The entire run cost only

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.640
a few thousand dollars on an academic scale budget. Last month, physicist and writer Four

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:41.240
Gravitons had challenged anyone to push past the prior eight-loop record. The full account

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:47.720
now sits on the Anthropic Science blog. Andre Carpathi posted that dropping the word artificial

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:54.920
from AGI and ASI has been standard terminology for a decade. He described the shorter forms as

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.040
cleaner because the prefix is redundant.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.000
The remark responded to ongoing discussion

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.940
about trajectories beyond current frontier systems.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.220
Simon Willison wrote that the last year in technology

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:08.880
has felt like 100 years compressed together.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:12.200
He added that every limit frontier models encounter

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.140
collapses within roughly a month.

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.360
Willison posted the observation the same morning

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:20.120
he delivered the closing keynote at VR developers.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.360
He also predicted that everything

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:24.240
done with frontier models today

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.720
will become instantaneous and free within a few years.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:32.420
Google set Gemini 3.5 Flash as the new default model

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:33.820
for AI mode globally.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:37.980
Sundar Pichai stated that Flash runs four times faster

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:40.420
than other frontier models while delivering

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:43.320
frontier-level performance at less than half the price.

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:47.600
AI mode has now passed 1 billion monthly active users.

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:51.120
Pichai also noted that AI overviews now

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.520
reached 2,500 million users.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:02:00.380
The company reported infrastructure spending of $180 to $190 billion for 2026.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.800
Willis and Post did that he would be on stage for the keynote in 10 minutes.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:09.360
The slot was the closing keynote on the main stage at We Are Developers.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:13.300
The Post gathered 28,600 views within hours.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:19.560
Google announced information agents that run persistent 24-7 background monitoring across

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:26.060
web, blogs, and real-time feeds. Users describe apartment requirements once and receive

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:32.080
synthesized matches with action capabilities. Expanded agentic booking now aggregates

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:37.680
real-time pricing and lets Google call businesses on the user's behalf for categories such as

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:44.280
home repair. Agentic coding inside search builds custom generative UI on the fly using

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:47.480
Gemini 3.5 flash and anti-gravity.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:52.780
Information agents launch first for Google AI Pro and ultra-subscribers.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:58.440
Custom anti-gravity mini-apps will follow for the same subscriber tiers in coming months.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:04.960
Microsoft Autopilot continues executing workplace tasks after the initial user prompt ends.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:10.480
The system maintains ongoing agent sessions that operate autonomously across documents

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:11.400
and applications.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:17.320
Persistent sessions allow the agent to finish multi-step workflows without further input.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:24.500
Leaks show that Meta's new AI agent Muse used real people at call centers to complete phone-based tasks.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:29.620
The support was required for conversations current models could not finish independently.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:34.160
The revelation came from internal documents obtained by the publication.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:41.040
A Reddit post shares a curated list of papers on data, tensor, pipeline, and model parallelism.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:46.320
The author includes a GitHub repository with basic implementations for each technique.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:52.140
The collection aims to give practitioners enough background to start coding distributed setups quickly.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:57.160
The post recommends reading the papers then immediately coding the referenced implementations.

00:03:57.160 --> 00:04:05.600
Pro action used Codex, GPT Live 1, and GPT 6 Astra to build, operate, and sell fleet

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:06.680
management software.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:13.360
The company recorded a 60% sales increase and saved more than 75 hours per week on development

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:13.860
tasks.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:19.840
The models handled code generation, operations automation, and sales workflow acceleration.

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:26.300
The latent space podcast episode covers open router's path from seed round to a reported

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.920
$7 billion acquisition by Stripe.

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:34.400
The discussion focuses on infrastructure for routing across dozens of frontier and open

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:35.100
wait models.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:42.100
Pipeline parallelism splits a model across multiple GPUs so that different layers run on different

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:46.140
devices and micro batches flow through the stages like an assembly line.

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:52.160
The approach reduces the memory footprint on any single GPU, compared with placing the

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:53.760
entire model on one card.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:59.220
Bubble time appears when a stage finishes its micro batch before the next stage is ready,

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:06.120
lowering overall utilization. With eight stages, the bubble fraction can reach 25% unless the

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:12.320
micro batch size is increased to keep every stage busy. Activation checkpointing trades extra

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:18.540
computation for lower memory use, cutting peak memory by roughly half at the cost of 30% more

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:25.160
flops. Teams choose pipeline parallelism when model size exceeds single GPU memory, yet

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:30.400
tensor parallelism would require expensive high bandwidth interconnects. The practical

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:36.720
rule is to start with pipeline stages equal to the number of GPUs, and then add tensor parallelism

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:42.760
inside each stage only when communication latency becomes the bottleneck. Eight stage pipelines

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:48.260
therefore require careful micro-batch tuning to avoid the 25% utilization penalty.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:53.160
Checkpointing remains the first lever teams adjust when memory pressure appears

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:55.600
before they increase interconnect spend.

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:59.680
Try the distributed algorithms repository from the Reddit post

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:03.800
to implement basic tensor and pipeline parallelism on a small model.

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:10.340
Test Gemini 3.5 flash inside Google AI mode for generative UI tasks

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:16.520
that previously required separate coding tools, run a persistent autopilot session on a multi-step

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:23.200
document workflow to see how it continues after the initial prompt. Explore the open router routing

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:29.820
options now that the platform has been acquired by Stripe for $7 billion. Google plans to expand

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:35.980
information agents to more subscriber tiers later this summer. Custom anti-gravity mini-apps

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:40.120
inside search are scheduled to reach AI pro users in the coming months.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:45.960
Open router users can expect continued routing improvements as more labs release new models.

